  "caption_groups": [
    {
      "start": 0.852083,
      "end": 2.870333,
      "text": "Beavers, the world’s most industrious"
    },
    {
      "start": 2.896375,
      "end": 5.266166,
      "text": "rodents, reshape rivers by building dams"
    },
    {
      "start": 5.292208,
      "end": 7.20625,
      "text": "that flood valleys, create wetlands,"
    },
    {
      "start": 7.3625,
      "end": 8.924999,
      "text": "and nurture diverse species."
    },
    {
      "start": 10.648083,
      "end": 12.275707999999998,
      "text": "Through relentless tree harvesting,"
    },
    {
      "start": 12.497041,
      "end": 14.658541,
      "text": "beavers obtain building material and food,"
    },
    {
      "start": 14.827791,
      "end": 17.197582999999998,
      "text": "dramatically altering forest structure along"
    },
    {
      "start": 17.223625,
      "end": 19.176749,
      "text": "riverbanks and influencing water flow"
    },
    {
      "start": 19.18975,
      "end": 20.322583,
      "text": "patterns downstream."
    },
    {
      "start": 21.652083,
      "end": 23.956791000000003,
      "text": "The Eurasian beaver ( Castor fiber) and"
    },
    {
      "start": 23.982833,
      "end": 26.430749,
      "text": "North American beaver ( Castor canadensis)"
    },
    {
      "start": 26.547916,
      "end": 28.110416,
      "text": "belong to the family Castoridae,"
    },
    {
      "start": 28.30575,
      "end": 31.027082,
      "text": "genus Castor, as recognized by scientific"
    },
    {
      "start": 31.053125,
      "end": 32.003666,
      "text": "classification."
    },
    {
      "start": 33.328083,
      "end": 34.473957999999996,
      "text": "Their dams slow water,"
    },
    {
      "start": 34.66925,
      "end": 36.804666000000005,
      "text": "raising local water tables and fostering"
    },
    {
      "start": 36.817666,
      "end": 39.2005,
      "text": "riparian vegetation that stabilizes banks"
    },
    {
      "start": 39.213499999999996,
      "end": 41.244791,
      "text": "while reducing erosion during floods."
    },
    {
      "start": 42.580082999999995,
      "end": 44.87174999999999,
      "text": "Created wetlands become nurseries for fish,"
    },
    {
      "start": 45.067083,
      "end": 47.46291599999999,
      "text": "amphibians, and waterfowl, increasing"
    },
    {
      "start": 47.488958,
      "end": 49.363958,
      "text": "regional biodiversity dramatically"
    },
    {
      "start": 49.38999999999999,
      "end": 51.538416,
      "text": "supporting insects, mammals, and plant"
    },
    {
      "start": 51.564457999999995,
      "end": 52.619166,
      "text": "communities alike."
    },
    {
      "start": 53.94408299999999,
      "end": 56.24879099999999,
      "text": "Flooded soils accumulate organic matter,"
    },
    {
      "start": 56.45712499999999,
      "end": 58.566498999999986,
      "text": "sequestering carbon and contributing to"
    },
    {
      "start": 58.57949999999999,
      "end": 60.66283199999999,
      "text": "climate regulation over decades making"
    },
    {
      "start": 60.68887499999999,
      "end": 62.81129099999999,
      "text": "beaver habitats valuable carbon sinks"
    },
    {
      "start": 62.837332999999994,
      "end": 63.527457999999996,
      "text": "worldwide."
    },
    {
      "start": 64.85208299999998,
      "end": 66.92241599999998,
      "text": "These engineered wetlands improve water"
    },
    {
      "start": 66.94845799999999,
      "end": 68.74533199999999,
      "text": "quality by filtering sediments and"
    },
    {
      "start": 68.77137499999999,
      "end": 71.31041599999999,
      "text": "nutrients, offering natural flood mitigation"
    },
    {
      "start": 71.336458,
      "end": 73.289583,
      "text": "for nearby communities and enhancing"
    },
    {
      "start": 73.30262499999999,
      "end": 74.799999,
      "text": "recreational opportunities."
    },
    {
      "start": 76.14408299999998,
      "end": 78.55295699999999,
      "text": "Thus, beavers act as keystone engineers,"
    },
    {
      "start": 78.80033299999998,
      "end": 81.22224899999999,
      "text": "reshaping rivers and sustaining ecosystems"
    },
    {
      "start": 81.24824999999998,
      "end": 83.357624,
      "text": "that countless species, including humans,"
    },
    {
      "start": 83.565958,
      "end": 85.49304099999999,
      "text": "rely upon for generations to come."
    }
  ],
